text = "Version 0.1: 9/2/26
Description:
- added menu with credits and version notes
- add wpi animation

Version 0.2: 9/9/26
Description:
- point and shoot gameplay
-credits and upgrades
- oxygen meter added
- room development
- obstacle development
- menu buttons on credits  and version notes
- New spritesheet for future intro sequence
bug fixes 

Version 0.3: 9/16/26
- tile sets created
- intro animation created
- more upgrades
- updated sprites
- Implemented sprites with animations
- updated menu art
- crates started

Version 0.4: 9/23/26
-crates added
-more tilesets created
-fixed duplicate upgrade bug and debugged upgrades
-bosses added (general and robot)
-more upgrades(health, bullet size and speed)
- added text to intro sequence along with a skip button
- added background music that loops
- Created a 3rd room (will be fully implemented for the next sprint, we had some issues with implementing it)

Version 0.5 9/30/26
- more tilesets created
- two completed planets/rooms that are filled with randomly spawning enemies and obstacles
- new enemy type (drone and turrets)
- teleporter on each (this is still very buggy. Changing to the actual levels from the test rooms caused some problems). The primary goal for the next sprint is to fix this, it doesnt always work or has unintended effects)
- updated intro sequence
- new final boss sprite created 
- key system for teleporter
- tutorial screen added
- Improved UI with EX icon

Version 0.6 final
- Added a new moon and Ice floor
- Changed the core game loop to traverse the worlds to find the teleporter/cave which brings you to a Boss arena where after you fight the boss you move to the next floor
- Added a new tileset for the slime arena
- Final boss implemented
- Added a \"Thank you for playing screen\" and a fade to black that happens after you beat the final boss
- Improved the teleporter system. Now functional and not as buggy as before
- General bug fixes and world improvements 
- Added a pause screen
- Fixed a bug with the credits scene
"
